ther or not  the string that you have like string 1  apples and oranges are terrible blah  blah blah whether or not it includes a  smaller string that you specify so here  let's run through some examples log we  run this just call this s so of the  sentence here does include the word  orange but it doesn't include the word  mango includes goes and looks inside the  sentence and it checks whether or not  the substring that you specify is  included in the sentence or the text now  we're gonna go look at starts with and  ends with  you can probably guess what these do  they're gonna check whether or not the  string starts with or ends with a  specific substring that you specify so  here we go okay remember that the  substring doesn't have to be a full word  it can be it can be a sentence a smaller  sentence on its own it can be just part  of a word it's just some string that  you're looking for now we go and run  this and you can see that the string  both started with the word Apple and  ends with hate them now one interesting  thing to note here is that these are  case sensitive so watch this reload and  you can see this fails because in the  original sentence a was capitalized but  we looked for a lowercase Apple now the  next method we're going to look for is  replaced and what this does is it it  goes through your string and it looks  for a specific substring that you  specify and then it replaces it with  another one that you specify so let's  take an example here we're gonna go for  oranges and we're gonna replace that  with pears go hit reload apples and  pears are terrible and I hate them and  just like the other and just like and  just like the previous examples these  are case sensitive as well the next on  the list is trimmed  and what this does is it trims  whitespace from both the beginning and  the end of the string now whitespace if  you haven't if you haven't heard of that  is the name given to text like spaces  tabs that kind of thing a use case for  t